  m_Name: Nation_Mexica_(Aztec)
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Colonization.Runtime::Colonization.NativeNationData
  displayName: Mexica (Aztec)
  leader: Moctezuma II
  date: c. 1519
  biography: Moctezuma II was the Mexica tlatoani at the arrival of Cortes in 1519. The city icon uses masonry buildings, twin temple shrines, canals and chinampa gardens.
  region: Basin of Mexico; Tenochtitlan and the wider Mexica tribute network.
  terrain:
  - Plain
  - Prairie
  - Swamp
  goods:
  - Food
  - Cotton
  jobs:
  - Farmers
  - Cotton Planters
  rival: Tlaxcalteca
  scenarioAggression: High
  contextNote: Cotton includes exchange and tribute from warmer regions; it does not imply cotton plantations in the highland capital. Tlaxcalteca is a documented rival polity.
  sources:
  - https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/tenochtitlan
  - https://82nd-and-fifth.metmuseum.org/toah/ht/08/canm.html
  - https://lugares.inah.gob.mx/en/pagina-de-elemento/2314
